  "live_records": {
    "q-168003": {
      "dom_id": "question-168003",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the area of a circle of radius $2?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of a circle is\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the radius $r=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
