    "q-168004": {
      "dom_id": "question-168004",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "${\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The graph consists of $4$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,-2],$ the arc of the quarter circle for $x\\in [-2,0]\\,,$ the line segment for $x\\in [0,\\frac{5}{2}]\\,,$ and the line segment for $x\\in [\\frac{5}{2},5]\\,.$\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-5}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{5/2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{5/2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{4}}\n$$\n\nThe $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,-2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,0]\\,.$ The corresponding region is a quarter circle. In part 1, we found the area of the circle as $A=4\\pi .$ So we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4\\pi  \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,\\frac{5}{2}]\\,.$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [\\frac{5}{2},5]\\,.$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+(-{A}_{2})+(-{A}_{3})+{A}_{4} \\\\  & =3-\\pi -\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =3-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
