    "q-168005": {
      "dom_id": "question-168005",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "If ${\\int }_{-8}^{-5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\pi -3,$ then ${\\int }_{-8}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
      "worked_solution": "From part $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3-\\pi ,\n$$\n\nand from the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-8}^{-5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-8}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\pi -3+3-\\pi =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
