    "q-168006": {
      "dom_id": "question-168006",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}({f}^{′}(x)-\\sqrt{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We split the integral into the sum of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({f}^{′}(x)-\\sqrt{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x-\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(x)\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}-\\sqrt{3}x\\,{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =(f(0)-f(-1))-\\sqrt{3}(0-(-1)) \\\\  & =(-2-(-\\sqrt{3}))-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2+\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
